From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tyn <tyn@localhost>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 11:25:26 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] tyn: sg-pc phone indicator, opening the phone by mouse /
 touch, attachments, 10:38

From the original Game.exe:

- The small phone at the top left of the scene (0x45a9a0, drawn over all layers like the original): date and day
  of the week (GlobalVars[1430]), antenna, battery, unread mark, "new mail" blinking over the date, the notice of
  flag 2617, the caller of an incoming call (name, or the number in small digits). Flag 2616 shows it.
- Opening the phone without a keyboard or pad (0x434d40, phone part): in the mouse mode a click / tap on the small
  phone (or the middle button) raises flag 2363, which the main loop of _STARTUP_WIN turns into the phone. The
  request stays up a few frames and the click is taken before the dialogue sees it, otherwise the message would
  advance and the scripts drop the request (they only open the phone while flag 1611 says the player is waited for).
  New hook UI::GameSpecific::UpdateInput, right after the pad input is read. 10:3F 13 / 14 turn the scene areas on /
  off; they are on after a load as well (13 only runs on a new start).
- Dial pad keys by mouse / touch (hit areas 34..45).
- Attachments: the phone's big screen behind pictures (0x44f840) and picture stories (0x44f980, PACG), text pages
  (0x44d120) with their scroll arrows; 10:38 (0x4683e0) sets the page table and drives the mouse scrolling of text
  pages and script scrolled mails (was a stub). Sheet 15 is PACG.

Checked on MuMu (Android 15, not a real device, original English data): Daru's "where did I put my phone" loop
(SG01_12) by taps only: small phone -> new mail opens -> back -> address book -> PhoneWave -> call -> "Call
complete."; dial pad 120# by taps.

Not done: the petals of the special attachment, the camera view of mode 12.

TYN only.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

